The first equality follow because $\left\vert A\right\vert \langle
\Phi|_{A^{\prime}A}\left(  \bbm{1}_{A^{\prime}}\otimes M_{AB}\right)  |\Phi
\rangle_{A^{\prime}A}=\operatorname{Tr}_{A}\{M_{AB}\}$ for any operator
$M_{AB}$. The second equality follows by applying the conjugate transpose of
\eqref{eq:ricochet-prop}. The final equality follows from the covariance
property of the channel.

Thus, if the receivers finally perform the unitaries $\bigotimes_{a\in\msc{A}}{W}_{A_a}^{\vv{g}}\otimes\bigotimes_{c\in\msc{C}}{W}_{C_c}^{\vv{g}}$ upon receiving $\vv{g}$ via a classical channel from the
